{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q23636392","formula":"NaPb₂(CO₃)₂(OH)","hill":"C2HNaO7Pb2","elements":["H","C","O","Na","Pb"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":1.0,"O":7.0,"Na":1.0,"Pb":2.0},"names":{"en":"Abellaite","uk":"Абеллаїт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Abellaite is a hydrous carbonate mineral discovered in the abandoned Eureka uranium mine in the village of La Torre de Capdella (Lleida province), Catalonia, Spain. The ideal chemical formula of abellaite is NaPb2(CO3)2(OH). It is named in honor of Joan Abella i Creus, a Catalan gemmologist who has long studied minerals from the Eureka mine and first found abellaite in the mine.","uk":"Абеллаїт — гідрокарбонатний мінерал, виявлений у покинутому урановому руднику «Еврика» в селі Торре-де-Капделла (провінція Леріда), Каталонія, Іспанія. Ідеальна хімічна формула абеллаїту — NaPb2(CO3)2(OH). Він названий на честь Джоана Абелла-і-Креуса, каталонського гемолога, який тривалий час вивчав мінерали з рудника «Еврика» і вперше знайшов у копальні абеллаїт."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q23636392","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abellaite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%97%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abellaite-738453.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q24629144","formula":"HNO₄Pb","names":{"ru":"Гидроксид-нитрат свинца(II)"},"elements":["H","N","O","Pb"],"fame":1,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q656004","formula":"C₂H₂O₈Pb₃","names":{"e